whisper: Dodge! Move with the left and right arrow keys and dodge the falling balls.
whisper: Run it with: cosmonova examples/dodge.cosmos      (or build it: cosmonova build examples/dodge.cosmos)

use: window

a ball has:
  birth (a flat place)
  speed (a number)
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  open a world with "Dodge!", 480, 640
  set player x to 240
  set balls to a list of balls
  set score to 0
  set best to 0
  try:
    load best from file "dodge best.json"
  if that went wrong:
    set best to 0
  set playing to yes
  as long as the world lives:
    if playing:
      if key held "left": set player x to player x minus 6
      if key held "right": set player x to player x plus 6
      set player x to clamp player x between 30 and 450
      if random number from 1 to 20 is 1: add a falling ball to balls
      set balls to every ball moved down from balls
      for each ball in balls:
        if hits the player with (ball, player x): set playing to no
      if not playing and score exceeds best:
        set best to score
        save best to file "dodge best.json"
      set score to score plus 1
    otherwise if key held "space":
      set balls to a list of balls
      set score to 0
      set playing to yes
    consume the window with "#101828"
    for each ball in balls: etch a circle with existence of ball of horizontal, existence of ball of vertical, 14, "orange"
    etch a box with player x minus 30, 600, 60, 16, "#5ad1ff"
    etch words with "Score: " plus score, 12, 10, "white"
    etch words with "Best: " plus best, 380, 10, "white"
    if not playing: etch words with "Ouch! Press space to play again.", 120, 300, "yellow"
    reveal the frame
and the universe said i love you

to a falling ball, returning a ball:
  set made to conjure a ball
  set birth of made to (random number from 20 to 460) horizontal -20 vertical
  set speed of made to random number from 3 to 8
  return made
and the universe said i love you

to every ball moved down from, given balls (a list of balls), returning a list of balls:
  set still falling to a list of balls
  for each ball in balls:
    set moved to ball
    set existence of moved to existence of ball plus 0 horizontal (speed of ball) vertical
    if existence of moved of vertical falls below 680: add moved to still falling
  return still falling
and the universe said i love you

to hits the player, given ball (a ball) and player x (a number), returning yes or no:
  set where to existence of ball
  return where of vertical exceeds 586 and where of vertical falls below 630 and where of horizontal is within 44 of player x
and the universe said i love you
